Sheltie ROI report · acme/widgets
30 landings on main, 2027-01-15 to 2027-01-15

  4 d 13 h less waiting and 30 fewer CI runs than a one-at-a-time merge queue

                            One at a time        Sheltie
  Waiting, total                 4 d 13 h            0 s
  Waiting, median              3 h 31 min            0 s
  Waiting, 90th percentile     6 h 19 min            0 s
  Extra CI runs                        30              0

With Sheltie, of 30 changes
     30  land as soon as they are ready
      0  rebuild on the new head first
      0  build together with a conflicting change
      0  go to the merge engine (same targets written)

Parallelism
  27 agents at once keep 80% of changes landing on their own
      1  conflicting pair through t0
      1  conflicting pair through t1
      1  conflicting pair through t2

Assumptions
  · 30 landings on main from 2027-01-15 to 2027-01-15, each ready when it landed.
  · CI takes 15 min per run, and every run passes.
  · Footprints predicted from changed files.
  · Waiting is wall-clock time from ready to landed; the pull requests' own CI is the same in both queues and not counted.
  · 2 landings without a footprint left out.
